<title>USA: Physician Corp Q3 loss widens with charge.</title>
<headline>Physician Corp Q3 loss widens with charge.</headline>
<dateline>MIAMI 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr    loss		$2.44     loss	 $0.03</p>
<p> Net    loss	     95,514     loss	 1,209</p>
<p> Revs		     362,080		  310,537</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  39,207		   39,326</p>
<p>	  Nine months</p>
<p> Shr     loss	     $2.41   profit	 $0.30</p>
<p> Net     loss	    95,112   profit	11,874</p>
<p> Revs		   1,089,192		  885,909</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  39,406		   39,954</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTES: 1996 third quarter includes a one-time after-tax $100 million or $2.55 per share workers' compensation business charge and a one-time $0.11 per share gain from the sale of the Georgia/Alabama HMOs.</p>
<p>The company said it continues to have discussions with its bankers regarding the financial covenants and repayment terms of its $118.5 million bank loan. The company expects to repay the loan upon closing its merger with Sierra Health Services Inc.</p>
</text>
